// EXPECT: [E003]
// Lock D-31: an array of resources that is simply dropped is a LEAK.
//
// This was accepted with no diagnostic at all by the sovereign engine while
// `--engine=legacy` reported it — a regression in the shipping default that no gate
// could see, because both engines pass the corpus. The cause was that `ir_alloca`
// marks a local slot as owning its contents and `ir_alloca_array` did not, and the
// leak check is gated on that bit, so no array-typed local ever entered it.
//
// `[T; N]` is linear iff `T` is (spec/chapters/07-types.tex), so `a` carries the
// release obligation of both its elements and discharges neither.

type R { mov h *u8 }

func main() i32 {
    var p *u8 = 0
    var a R[2] = [R(p), R(p)]
    return 0
}
